# User-level (client-side) nix config. Daemon-level settings like
# trusted-users / substituters / experimental-features are managed
# declaratively by the flake (nix.settings in modules/infra/nix/ on
# NixOS, determinate module on nix-darwin) — don't duplicate them here.
#
# `auto-optimise-store` is a *restricted* setting, which normally means it
# should not live in a user-level (client) config: a client that sends it
# without being trusted gets every store operation prefixed with "warning:
# ignoring the client-specified setting 'auto-optimise-store', because it is a
# restricted setting and you are not a trusted user" — once per connection,
# which is where the flood in `nix develop` came from.
#
# It is nonetheless set below on purpose, because this file is the ONLY channel
# that reaches the macOS hosts. There, nix-darwin's own nix module is
# force-disabled and Determinate Nixd owns /etc/nix/nix.conf outright, so the
# flake's nix.settings do NOT apply (modules/infra/nix/* registers only as
# my.modules.nixos; see the header comment in modules/infra/darwin-builder.nix).
# On those hosts ashebanow is listed explicitly in
# determinateNix.customSettings.trusted-users, so the setting is accepted —
# no warning, and it takes effect.
#
# On the NixOS hosts the flake declares it daemon-side
# (modules/infra/nix/nix.nix), which is what actually governs store
# operations there. The line below is then accepted too (wheel is trusted via
# nix.settings.trusted-users) and agrees with the daemon, so it is harmless.
# Do not delete it as "duplication": that would silently drop the setting on
# macOS, where this file is the only way to set it.
#
# (The GitHub access-token line that used to live here was deleted in
# BOX-170: it did nothing, because no private flake input exists and a
# user-level nix.conf is never forwarded to the daemon. See
# docs/research/nix-config-github-token-redundancy.md.)

accept-flake-config = true
auto-optimise-store = true
cores = 8
max-jobs = auto

extra-experimental-features = nix-command flakes
